---
title: Tokens
order: 1
description: Colour, type, space and motion tokens for the Calico Melton shop.
---
{%- macro tokenTable(list, caption) -%}
<div class="docs-table-wrap">
  <table class="docs-table">
    <caption class="ds-visually-hidden">{{ caption }}</caption>
    <thead><tr><th scope="col">Token</th><th scope="col">Value</th><th scope="col">Notes</th></tr></thead>
    <tbody>
      {%- for t in list %}
      <tr>
        <th scope="row"><code>{{ t.cssVar }}</code></th>
        <td><code>{{ t.value }}</code>{% if t.alias %}<span class="docs-alias">→ {{ t.alias }}</span>{% endif %}</td>
        <td>{{ t.description or "" }}</td>
      </tr>
      {%- endfor %}
    </tbody>
  </table>
</div>
{%- endmacro -%}

{%- macro swatches(list, prefix) -%}
<ul class="docs-swatches" role="list">
  {%- for t in list %}
  <li class="docs-swatch">
    <span class="docs-swatch__chip" style="--chip: var({{ t.cssVar }})"></span>
    <span class="docs-swatch__name">{{ t.path | tokenTail(prefix) }}</span>
    <code class="docs-swatch__value">{{ t.value }}</code>
    {%- if t.alias %}<span class="docs-alias">→ {{ t.alias }}</span>{% endif %}
    {%- if t.description %}<span class="docs-swatch__note">{{ t.description }}</span>{% endif %}
    <code class="docs-swatch__var">{{ t.cssVar }}</code>
  </li>
  {%- endfor %}
</ul>
{%- endmacro -%}

<header class="docs-header">
  <p class="docs-eyebrow">Design system · Layer 1</p>
  <h1>Tokens</h1>
  <p class="docs-lede">Every colour, size and timing on the site comes from here. Values are taken from the current calicomelton.com, which takes its colours from the paintings.</p>
</header>

<nav class="docs-toc" aria-label="On this page">
  <ul role="list">
    <li><a href="#tiers">Tiers</a></li>
    <li><a href="#colour">Colour</a></li>
    <li><a href="#contrast">Contrast</a></li>
    <li><a href="#type">Type</a></li>
    <li><a href="#space">Space</a></li>
    <li><a href="#size">Size</a></li>
    <li><a href="#shape">Radius, border, shadow</a></li>
    <li><a href="#motion">Motion</a></li>
    <li><a href="#layers-z">Z-index</a></li>
    <li><a href="#breakpoints">Breakpoints</a></li>
    <li><a href="#ratios">Image ratios</a></li>
    <li><a href="#component">Component tokens</a></li>
  </ul>
</nav>

<section class="docs-section" aria-labelledby="tiers">
  <h2 id="tiers">Tiers</h2>
  <dl class="docs-tiers">
    <div><dt>Primitive</dt><dd>Raw values, like <code>color.maroon.600</code> or <code>space.4</code>. Components never use these directly.</dd></div>
    <div><dt>Semantic</dt><dd>What a value is for, like <code>color.text.muted</code> or <code>space.stack.md</code>. Most component CSS uses these.</dd></div>
    <div><dt>Component</dt><dd>A knob for a single component, like <code>button.radius</code>. Added only when a component needs one.</dd></div>
  </dl>
  <p>Source: <code>tokens/{primitive,semantic,component}/*.json</code>. Output: <code>src/styles/tokens.css</code>, {{ designTokens.length }} custom properties.</p>
</section>

<section class="docs-section" aria-labelledby="colour">
  <h2 id="colour">Colour</h2>
  <p>A calm cream page lets the paintings lead. Pink is for bands like the Studio Letter. Blue, pink and maroon are accents for small moments, never large fills.</p>

  <h3>Semantic</h3>
  {%- for group in ["surface", "text", "border", "action", "status", "accent", "focus", "scrim"] %}
  <h4 class="docs-subhead">{{ group }}</h4>
  {{ swatches(designTokens | tokensAt("color." ~ group, "semantic"), "color." ~ group) }}
  {%- endfor %}

  <h3>Primitive</h3>
  {{ swatches(designTokens | tokensAt("color", "primitive"), "color") }}
</section>

<section class="docs-section" aria-labelledby="contrast">
  <h2 id="contrast">Contrast</h2>
  <p>Every colour pairing the system allows, checked against WCAG 2.2 AA on each build (<code>npm run contrast</code>). Text needs 4.5:1. Control edges and focus rings need 3:1. A pairing that isn't listed here isn't allowed: add it to <code>scripts/contrast-pairs.js</code> first.</p>
  <div class="docs-table-wrap">
    <table class="docs-table docs-contrast">
      <caption class="ds-visually-hidden">Colour contrast checks</caption>
      <thead><tr><th scope="col">Sample</th><th scope="col">Foreground on background</th><th scope="col">Ratio</th><th scope="col">Result</th></tr></thead>
      <tbody>
        {%- for c in contrast %}
        <tr>
          <td><span class="docs-contrast__sample" style="--fg: var({{ c.fgVar }}); --bg: var({{ c.bgVar }})">Aa</span></td>
          <th scope="row"><code>{{ c.fg }}</code> on <code>{{ c.bg }}</code></th>
          <td>{{ c.ratio }}:1 <span class="docs-muted">(needs {{ c.min }})</span></td>
          <td>{{ "Pass" if c.pass else "Fail" }}</td>
        </tr>
        {%- endfor %}
      </tbody>
    </table>
  </div>
</section>

<section class="docs-section" aria-labelledby="type">
  <h2 id="type">Type</h2>
  <p>Lora for headings and the wordmark, Figtree for everything else. Sizes are fluid: they grow with the screen between a set minimum and maximum, and still scale with browser zoom.</p>

  <h3>Roles</h3>
  {%- set roles = [
    { prefix: "type.display", label: "Display", sample: "Calico Melton" },
    { prefix: "type.heading.xl", label: "Heading XL", sample: "New paintings" },
    { prefix: "type.heading.lg", label: "Heading LG", sample: "Sign up for new work" },
    { prefix: "type.heading.md", label: "Heading MD", sample: "You're on the list." },
    { prefix: "type.heading.sm", label: "Heading SM", sample: "Edition of 25, giclée on cotton rag" },
    { prefix: "type.body", label: "Body", sample: "New paintings, studio notes, and first access to prints. I'll send the next one straight to your inbox." },
    { prefix: "type.label", label: "Label", sample: "Email address" },
    { prefix: "type.small", label: "Small", sample: "Unsubscribe any time." },
    { prefix: "type.eyebrow", label: "Eyebrow", sample: "The Studio Letter", upper: true }
  ] %}
  {%- set cssProp = { "family": "font-family", "size": "font-size", "weight": "font-weight", "line-height": "line-height", "tracking": "letter-spacing" } %}
  <div class="docs-type-roles">
    {%- for role in roles %}
    {%- set parts = designTokens | tokensAt(role.prefix) %}
    <div class="docs-type-role">
      <p class="docs-type-role__sample{% if role.upper %} docs-type-role__sample--upper{% endif %}" style="
        {%- for t in parts %}{% set key = t.path | tokenTail(role.prefix) %}{% if cssProp[key] %}{{ cssProp[key] }}: var({{ t.cssVar }}); {% endif %}{% endfor %}">{{ role.sample }}</p>
      <p class="docs-type-role__meta"><strong>{{ role.label }}</strong>
        {%- for t in parts %} <code>{{ t.cssVar }}</code>{% endfor %}</p>
    </div>
    {%- endfor %}
  </div>

  <h3>Size scale</h3>
  <ul class="docs-scale" role="list">
    {%- for t in designTokens | tokensAt("font.size") %}
    <li><span class="docs-scale__label"><code>{{ t.cssVar }}</code><span class="docs-muted">{{ t.value }}</span></span>
      <span class="docs-scale__sample" style="font-size: var({{ t.cssVar }})">Bristol painter</span></li>
    {%- endfor %}
  </ul>

  <h3>Families, weights, line heights, tracking</h3>
  {{ tokenTable(designTokens | tokensAtAny(["font.family", "font.weight", "font.line-height", "font.tracking"]), "Font primitives") }}
</section>

<section class="docs-section" aria-labelledby="space">
  <h2 id="space">Space</h2>
  <p>Steps 7 to 9 are fluid, so sections breathe more on big screens. <strong>Stack</strong> is vertical space between things, <strong>inset</strong> is padding inside, <strong>inline</strong> is horizontal space between things.</p>
  <ul class="docs-space" role="list">
    {%- for t in designTokens | tokensAt("space", "primitive") %}
    <li><code>{{ t.cssVar }}</code><span class="docs-space__bar" style="inline-size: var({{ t.cssVar }})"></span><span class="docs-muted">{{ t.value }}</span></li>
    {%- endfor %}
  </ul>
  <h3>Semantic</h3>
  {{ tokenTable(designTokens | tokensAt("space", "semantic"), "Semantic space") }}
</section>

<section class="docs-section" aria-labelledby="size">
  <h2 id="size">Size</h2>
  {{ tokenTable(designTokens | tokensAt("layout"), "Layout sizes") }}
  {{ tokenTable(designTokens | tokensAt("icon"), "Icon sizes") }}
  {{ tokenTable(designTokens | tokensAt("target"), "Touch target") }}
  <details class="docs-details"><summary>Primitives</summary>
  {{ tokenTable(designTokens | tokensAt("size"), "Size primitives") }}
  </details>
</section>

<section class="docs-section" aria-labelledby="shape">
  <h2 id="shape">Radius, border, shadow</h2>
  <ul class="docs-shapes" role="list">
    {%- for t in designTokens | tokensAt("shape") %}
    <li><span class="docs-shapes__box" style="border-radius: var({{ t.cssVar }})"></span><code>{{ t.cssVar }}</code><span class="docs-alias">→ {{ t.alias }}</span></li>
    {%- endfor %}
    {%- for t in designTokens | tokensAt("elevation") %}
    <li><span class="docs-shapes__box docs-shapes__box--raised" style="box-shadow: var({{ t.cssVar }})"></span><code>{{ t.cssVar }}</code><span class="docs-alias">→ {{ t.alias }}</span></li>
    {%- endfor %}
  </ul>
  {{ tokenTable(designTokens | tokensAt("line"), "Line widths") }}
  <details class="docs-details"><summary>Primitives</summary>
  {{ tokenTable(designTokens | tokensAt("radius"), "Radius primitives") }}
  {{ tokenTable(designTokens | tokensAt("border"), "Border primitives") }}
  {{ tokenTable(designTokens | tokensAt("shadow"), "Shadow primitives") }}
  </details>
</section>

<section class="docs-section" aria-labelledby="motion">
  <h2 id="motion">Motion</h2>
  <p>Quick and quiet. <strong>UI</strong> timing is for hovers and presses, <strong>panel</strong> timing is for the cart drawer and menus. All motion is switched off when someone asks their device for reduced motion.</p>
  <div class="docs-motion">
    {%- for kind in ["ui", "panel"] %}
    <button type="button" class="docs-motion__demo" style="--d: var(--ds-transition-{{ kind }}-duration); --e: var(--ds-transition-{{ kind }}-easing)">
      <span class="docs-motion__dot"></span><span>{{ kind | capitalize }}: hover or focus me</span>
    </button>
    {%- endfor %}
  </div>
  {{ tokenTable(designTokens | tokensAt("transition"), "Semantic motion") }}
  <details class="docs-details"><summary>Primitives</summary>
  {{ tokenTable(designTokens | tokensAt("motion"), "Motion primitives") }}
  </details>
</section>

<section class="docs-section" aria-labelledby="layers-z">
  <h2 id="layers-z">Z-index</h2>
  {{ tokenTable(designTokens | tokensAt("layer"), "Z-index layers") }}
</section>

<section class="docs-section" aria-labelledby="breakpoints">
  <h2 id="breakpoints">Breakpoints</h2>
  <p>Components should prefer container queries, so they adapt to the space they're given rather than the screen. CSS can't read custom properties inside <code>@media</code> or <code>@container</code>, so queries repeat these rem values. Stylelint allows rem in query conditions only.</p>
  {{ tokenTable(designTokens | tokensAt("breakpoint"), "Breakpoints") }}
</section>

<section class="docs-section" aria-labelledby="ratios">
  <h2 id="ratios">Image ratios</h2>
  <ul class="docs-ratios" role="list">
    {%- for t in designTokens | tokensAt("aspect") %}
    <li><span class="docs-ratios__frame" style="aspect-ratio: var({{ t.cssVar }})"></span><code>{{ t.cssVar }}</code><span class="docs-muted">{{ t.value }}{% if t.description %} · {{ t.description }}{% endif %}</span></li>
    {%- endfor %}
  </ul>
</section>

<section class="docs-section" aria-labelledby="component">
  <h2 id="component">Component tokens</h2>
  <p>Only where one component needs its own control.</p>
  {{ tokenTable(designTokens | tokensAtAny(["button", "product-card", "cart-drawer"]), "Component tokens") }}
</section>
